    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0289" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.796/393a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-09T16:00:00-04:00">August 9, 1941—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>175. Clayton requests following be communicated to Morgan:</p>
                <p>“The telegram from you sent on the 5th of August was received on the 8th.<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d226-f1"/> It is believed that every endeavor should be made
                    by you to have the purchase of assets and equipment of Sedta brought about at a
                    price which will be as low as possible. Such price should not be more than
                    $150,000 and should be on terms mentioned in discussion with you before you
                    left. Please let us know if this is not possible. With reference to the telegram
                    dated August 6,<anchor n="62" xml:id="d226-f2"/> please report the extent of
                    free transportation which Panagra provided as well as what further amount of
                    such transportation would be desired.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
